"text":"Regional symbols"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Regional symbol subscription receives events only from a designated exchange, marketplace, or venue"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instead of receiving composite events from all venues (by default). Regional symbol is composed from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"base symbol, ampersand character (’&’), and an exchange code character. For example,"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“SPY” is the symbol for composite events for SPDR S&P 500 ETF from all exchanges,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“SPY&N” is the symbol for event for SPDR S&P 500 ETF that originate only from NYSE marketplace."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Symbol attributes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Market event symbols can have a number of attributes attached to then in curly braces"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with “<key>=<value>” paris separated by commas. For example,"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“SPY{price=bid}” is the market symbol “SPY” with an attribute key “price” set to value “bid”."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“SPY(=5m,tho=true}” is the market symbol “SPY” with two attributes. One has an empty key and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value “5m”, while the other has key “tho” and value “true”."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The methods in this class always maintain attribute keys in alphabetic order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/docs.dxfeed.com\/dxfeed\/api\/com\/dxfeed\/event\/market\/MarketEventSymbols.html"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/dxfeedframework\/marketeventsymbols"]}],"hierarchy":